;smartlock_v2_beta_final*probably*
;Oj742
;
;A lock that checks polarity cycle and offset of the opponent to create an accurate lock
;It also skips clearing spaces where there is nothing
;
;Taking a page from omnipotence's book we have special casing
;for certain programs, though it is hopefully more generalized and less exploitable
;
;It uses a decoy instead of a flag for locking as it takes a good chunk of time determining if it has either
;a different clear than expected or a timer clear, in which case we go to bunker mode until I come up with a better strategy
;The time needed to do this isn't an issue: we'll have more than half the game left by the time we're done
;
;Side note: OHGODWHATAMIDOINGIHAVENOIDEAPLEASEHELP
;Side note2: It appears that my reliance on special casing has grown far larger than anticipated
;I should work on that eventually
;Side note3: Soon
;

>(+)*5>>+>>->(+)*5<<(-)*14<(+)*6<(-)*14<(+)*17<
;My god turtles are so annoying
(-)*42(>)*6(>[-[++[+[+[-----[-[(>)*1(>([(+)*8([-{[(-)*112[-.]>]}])%16])*2)*21
]]]]]]]+)*2(<)*5([{
;we've been waiting for some sort of enemy contact for 6210 cycles now so assume that the opponent is defensive or really really slow
;why 6210 cycles? its a number likely greater than the number of cycles it should take to detect an offensive program and it seems
;to be the magic number for racking up the most points against ais523_preparation

;Anti defence program code derived from Oj742_smart_timerclear
(>)*5(>[-[++[+[+[-----[-[(+)*14<<[(+)*11[-]]]]]]]]>][++[+.]]>
([-{[(+)*89[+.]]}>[-[++[+[+[-----[-[(+)*22<<[-]]]]]]]>][++[+.]]>
